<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ambrose</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 339–397</span> · Also known as Saint Ambrose, Ambrose of Milan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ambrose was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> from 374 and one of the four original Doctors of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-christendom">Latin Church</a>. A Roman governor chosen bishop by popular acclaim, he opposed the Arians, defended the Church's independence from emperors, made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a> do penance after the massacre at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessalonica</a> in 390, and baptised Augustine. He became the patron saint of Milan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ambrose.jpg" alt="Ambrose" width="306" height="336" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AmbroseOfMilan_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
